Z||000003||Hippocrat||09-17-2001||01:36 AM||||thanks for the info .. 88 GT the only one that had the getrag? really was the one I'm looking for ..getting ready to do a V8 swap and I as well heard that this was the stronger of the 5spds .. anybody know of any swaps done using the muncie? if so any idea how it held up ? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||09-17-2001||01:46 AM||||there were 3 kinds of Fiero manual tranny's, the muncie 4 speed, isuzu 5 speed, and getrag 5 speed.<P>The Muncie 4 speed came in all 84's and the 85-86 V6 cars.<P>The Isuzu 5 speed came in all 2.5l 4 cyl 85-88<P>The Getrag 5 speed came in late 86 GT's (and some SE's, I've heard) and all 87-88 2.8 v6's.<P>There's been some debate over which 5 speed is better, isuzu or getrag.. getrag is stronger, isuzu shifts better etc etc.  I think it's all a matter of opinion.  I have the getrag in my 86 GT and aside from a blown 3rd gear synchro it shifts fine, and I have an isuzu 5 speed (although it is from a 96 sunfire) in my quad Coupe, and it feels a bit notchier than my getrag.  But there's also a shortened shifter in the coupe, which increases shift effort a bit.  All comes down to personal preferance.  The Getrags are hard to find, and usually expensive.<P>oh yeah... as far as swaps, I've heard of more V8 swaps being done with the isuzu.  You shouldn't have a problem with any tranny so long as you don't do too many burnouts or powershifts.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hippocrat||09-17-2001||01:51 AM||||thanx guys thats pretty much what I wanted to know.. from the sounds of that I have one of each excluding the getrag .. figures but hey. ||||reg||1
